Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:11:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10192/11362] Record that 58% of ARC artifacts would fail their
 own lint if staged

Measured with the lint's own candidate selector: of 573 ARC artifacts, 194
declare an illegal inference_substrate and 141 declare none -- 335 of 573.
Plus 111 non-terminal verdicts, 56 un-allowlisted live-LLM claims, 53 missing
durations, 18 below their substrate floor.

The guard has been green because it is a pre-commit hook and result artifacts
are written once and never re-staged, so it has never inspected the population
it governs. Same structural blind spot CLAUDE.md documents for
operator_curated_docs_lint. It surfaced only because an unrelated sweep staged
157 old artifacts at once and three fell out; the real rate is 58%, not 2%.

The illegal values split three ways with three different fixes: genuine drift
(including hardware_smoke, which is in CLAUDE.md's own substrate table but not
in the code's allow-list -- prose and enforcement disagree), 23 that are
merely malformed (a legal name with a trailing comment), and three carrying
the exact string exp3946's comment records as fixed in the artifact but not in
the writer, so re-runs recreate it.

Recorded rather than fixed: the repair differs per class, and widening
SUBSTRATE_DURATION_FLOORS to make commits pass is what
substrate_alias_evidence_lint exists to catch.

